{
    "title": "Dimention Smasher",
    "subtitle": "Hardware and software system for expanding live streamers' creativity space",
    "type": "System Design",
    "location": "Hangzhou",
    "date": "02 FEB 24",
    "mainContent": [
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": "A **hardware + software system** for **live creators**: it **expands the creative space** beyond a flat camera frame—giving streamers **new spatial affordances** (layers, props, interactions) without forcing a heavier production pipeline.",
            "credits": ""
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Pain points"
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": "- **Single-plane** streaming flattens performance and novelty.\n- **Toolchains** that add depth often demand **studio-grade** skill and setup.\n- Creators need **playful iteration**, not only post-production polish.",
            "credits": ""
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Solution"
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": "**Dimension Smasher** couples **physical interfaces** with **real-time software**:\n\n- **Spatial smashing**: break the default rectangle into composable creative zones.\n- **Streamer-first loop**: fast try → observe chat feedback → adjust layout.\n- **System thinking**: firmware, visuals, and interaction cues stay **one product**.",
            "credits": ""
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Mental model"
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": "Creator **sets scene** → **hardware + software** remap space → **audience** reads a wider performance field → creator **tunes** live.",
            "credits": ""
        },
